# Deployment

**Do not use CDK** for deployments. Use only the specific deploy scripts in the `scripts/` folder.

## Scripts to Use

| Component | Script |
|-----------|--------|
| Backend (Lambda) | `./scripts/deploy-lambda-direct.sh` (updates **API handler** and, when `backend/lambda/loyalty-consumer.zip` exists after build, **warmpawz-dev-loyalty-events-consumer**) |
| Admin Web | `./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh` |
| Vendor Web | `./scripts/deploy-vendor-web.sh` |
| Customer Web | `./scripts/deploy-customer-web.sh` |

## Examples

```bash
# Deploy backend only (dev — default function warmpawz-dev-api-handler)
./scripts/deploy-lambda-direct.sh

# Deploy admin web only (dev)
./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh

# Deploy both backend and admin web (dev)
./scripts/deploy-lambda-direct.sh && ./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh
```

## Production (ship backend + admin)

Use the same scripts; prod is selected by **environment variable** (Lambda) and **`--prod`** (admin). Admin injects **prod HTTP API**: `https://mss9sa4y01.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com` (see `scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh`).

```bash
# 1) Backend → prod Lambda (ap-south-1)
LAMBDA_FUNCTION_NAME=warmpawz-prod-api-handler ./scripts/deploy-lambda-direct.sh

# 2) Admin web → prod S3 + CloudFront, runtime config → prod API Gateway
./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh --prod

# Non-interactive (e.g. CI): skip the "type yes" prompt
./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh --prod --yes

# Both in one line
LAMBDA_FUNCTION_NAME=warmpawz-prod-api-handler ./scripts/deploy-lambda-direct.sh && ./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh --prod
```

Alternate admin URL after deploy: `https://admin.warmpawz.com` (same CloudFront origin as `https://dbr09zyoq9akb.cloudfront.net`; see `prodscripts/PRODUCTION_CONFIG.md`).

## API Lambda environment (UAT / dev HTTP API)

The handler behind API Gateway (for example `warmpawz-dev-api-handler` on `https://z0b3obweb6.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com`) verifies **`warmpawz-uat` JWTs when `UAT_MODE=true` or when the token’s issuer claim is `warmpawz-uat`** (signature must match `UAT_JWT_SECRET`). Client headers such as `x-uat-mode` do not enable verification; see `backend/lambda/src/utils/jwt-verification.ts`.

- **`UAT_MODE`**: Set to `true` on the dev/UAT API Lambda when vendor or customer apps use UAT OTP (`123456`) and UAT-issuer tokens. Terraform dev sets this in `infra/envs/dev/main.tf` (`common_env_vars`). Serverless-based deploys read SSM `/warmpawz/<stage>/features/uatMode` (`backend/lambda/serverless.yml`); it must be the string `true` for UAT JWT acceptance.
- **`UAT_JWT_SECRET`**: HMAC secret for signing and verifying `warmpawz-uat` tokens (`backend/lambda/src/utils/jwt-generator.ts`). If unset, sign and verify both use the same built-in default on that process — but if you set it on one deploy path (AWS console, SSM, or Terraform variable `uat_jwt_secret` in dev), **every** code path that issues or checks those tokens on that Lambda must use the identical value. Optional Terraform: `infra/envs/dev/variables.tf` → `uat_jwt_secret` (merged into Lambda env when non-empty).

**Local** (`npm run start:local` / `serverless.local.yml`): use `UAT_MODE=true` in `.env.local` for UAT issuer tokens; set `UAT_JWT_SECRET` if you override the default and need parity with a remote API.
